#: ../../../advanced/build_wasm_emscripten.md:20
msgid ""
"If you would rather not manage the toolchain yourself, VTK ships wasm "
"presets that do it for you. They require only CMake 3.25 or newer, Ninja and "
"a python3 interpreter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/build_wasm_emscripten.md:23
msgid "cmake --workflow --preset wasm32   # or wasm64\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/build_wasm_emscripten.md:27
msgid ""
"That single command configures into `out/build/wasm32`, builds, and along "
"the way downloads an Emscripten SDK and a NodeJS if it cannot find any. The "
"first run therefore downloads roughly a gigabyte and takes several minutes. "
"There is no `emcmake`, no `emsdk_env` and no `PATH` to set: the presets use "
"a toolchain wrapper, `CMake/wasm/vtkEmscriptenToolchain.cmake`, which "
"resolves the SDK and passes the same two settings `emcmake` would have "
"(`CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE` and `CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/build_wasm_emscripten.md:34
msgid ""
"Downloaded tools go to a per-user cache rather than into the source tree, so "
"they are shared between build trees and checkouts:"
msgstr ""

