#: ../../../advanced/build_wasm_emscripten.md:343
msgid ""
"Let's breakdown the command. It is important to understand how the command "
"can be customized with additional arguments to the unit test. The above "
"command runs a CMake script `vtkWasmTestRunner.cmake` with the engine "
"argument pointing to `chrome`. Finally the cmake script script is given a "
"path to the test executable followed by arguments that will be passed to the "
"unit test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/build_wasm_emscripten.md:348
msgid ""
"If your test crashes with errors like \"Uncaught rejection from [object "
"Promise]: 3829048\", \"Received exit code 1\", \"Out of memory\", you can "
"force the test runner to keep the browser open by passing \"-"
"DEXIT_AFTER_TEST=OFF\". This is also required for asynchronous tests that "
"use JSPI."
msgstr ""
